    ],
    "function": "Catalyzes the phosphorylation of D-fructose 6-phosphate to fructose 1,6-bisphosphate by ATP, the first committing step of glycolysis. Can also catalyze the phosphorylation of tagatose-6-phosphate. The catalytic efficiency with tagatose-6-phosphate is about 1.8 times lower than that with fructose 6-phosphate. Can use phosphate donors other than ATP (GTP and ITP), with lower efficiency. In addition, can catalyze the reverse gluconeogenic reaction, albeit with low efficiency. May support and maintain basic glycolysis and metabolic fluxes during conditions inhibiting PfkA",
